course: dictionary
lesson: 4142
title: Glory and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Glory is a word with several meanings, so the clues around it tell you which one fits. In stories and sport, glory means great fame, honour and praise for doing something important or brave. In church, «Glory to God» means great praise and worship for God.
explain: Glory can also mean great beauty. In «the glory of the sunset», a sunset is something you look at, so glory means its wonderful beauty. Always ask: what does the sentence tell me about this word? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Glory can be a verb too. To glory in something means to enjoy it with great pride. The toads in the story are called the «Death-or-Glory Toads», and «die-hards» are fighters who never give up. Their name tells you they are ready to risk everything to win glory.
fact: Glory means great fame, honour and praise won by doing something important or brave.
fact: In church, glory means the great praise and worship given to God.
fact: Glory can also mean great beauty, as in «the glory of the sunset».
fact: To glory in something means to enjoy it with great pride.
fact: «Glory days» means happy times from the past.
exercise: «The Death-or-Glory Toads will storm the orchard.» What does glory mean in this name? | Walking very slowly | A dark and cold night | A sweet, juicy fruit | *Great fame and honour won by brave deeds
exercise: «the glory of the sunset» What does glory mean here? | *Great beauty | Great pride in losing a game | A type of cloud | A quiet, empty road
exercise: In church, people sing «Glory to God». What does glory mean here? | Loud shouting in a crowd | A big family meal | *Great praise and worship for God | A cheerful dance
test: Nadia says, «I glory in my new garden.» What does glory in mean? | To sell it | *To enjoy it with great pride | To cry about it | To forget it
test: What does «glory days» mean? | *Happy times from the past | Days at the seaside in winter | Days when it rains all week | Days when you are ill in bed
exam: Which of these is a meaning of glory? | A small, quiet whisper | *Great fame and honour won by doing something brave | A flat, empty field | Cold, grey rain
